			<item>
				<title>Stop using URL shorteners</title>
				<link>https://kowalcj0.github.io/2018/08/20/stop-using-url-shortners/</link>
				<pubDate>Mon, 20 Aug 2018 18:41:50 +0100</pubDate>
				<guid>https://kowalcj0.github.io/2018/08/20/stop-using-url-shortners/</guid>
				<description>&lt;p&gt;Why do people use URL shorteners?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;They&amp;rsquo;re simply unreliable and bad for privacy.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;I&amp;rsquo;ve already encountered quite a few dead short URLs because the URL shortener&#xA;service was closed down and it was rather painfull waste of time to find&#xA;the original link.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;They&amp;rsquo;re bad for privacy because the shortener service knows what are you browsing.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Why would give away such important meta data about your readers to someone else?&lt;/p&gt;</description>
			</item>
